1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,271
What if Earth had a ten-second rewind button?

2
00:00:03,311 --> 00:00:05,448
You spill coffee on your laptop,

3
00:00:05,488 --> 00:00:07,965
panic, and slap the big red button on

4
00:00:08,005 --> 00:00:08,917
the lamp post.

5
00:00:08,957 --> 00:00:10,618
The whole planet rewinds.

6
00:00:10,658 --> 00:00:13,067
The coffee flies back into your cup.

7
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:16,534
Everyone walks backward for ten seconds.

8
00:00:16,574 --> 00:00:17,424
Pigeons un-poop.

9
00:00:17,464 --> 00:00:18,869
A delivery truck un-honks.

10
00:00:18,909 --> 00:00:20,593
Nobody remembers it except you,

11
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:23,596
standing there holding the button like a magic remote.

12
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,808
You start fixing small things.

13
00:00:26,848 --> 00:00:28,276
A trip on the stairs.

14
00:00:28,316 --> 00:00:29,465
A typo in a text.

15
00:00:29,505 --> 00:00:30,654
An awkward hello.

16
00:00:30,694 --> 00:00:34,710
With ten seconds, you become the smoothest person in town.

17
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:37,789
Then everyone finds the button.

18
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:39,607
The queue stretches for miles.

19
00:00:39,647 --> 00:00:41,728
Every press undoes somebody else's,

20
00:00:41,768 --> 00:00:44,092
and the same ten seconds loop again and

21
00:00:44,132 --> 00:00:45,910
again, like a skipping record.

22
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:48,322
Arguments get weird.

23
00:00:48,362 --> 00:00:49,716
You say something rude,

24
00:00:49,756 --> 00:00:52,201
slap the button, and the words slide back

25
00:00:52,241 --> 00:00:53,171
into your mouth.

26
00:00:53,211 --> 00:00:57,110
Honestly, this should have been invented for every family dinner.

27
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:01,088
Scientists say a real rewind would need to

28
00:01:01,128 --> 00:01:03,270
reverse entropy itself, which is,

29
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:05,321
to put it politely, impossible.

30
00:01:05,361 --> 00:01:07,172
But as a thought experiment,

31
00:01:07,212 --> 00:01:09,024
it is a lovely idea to hold.

32
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:13,084
Twist: you are the only one who remembers.

33
00:01:13,124 --> 00:01:15,685
So you save the button for one moment:

34
00:01:15,725 --> 00:01:17,738
your niece's very first laugh.

35
00:01:17,778 --> 00:01:19,791
You rewind it again and again,

36
00:01:19,831 --> 00:01:21,639
until the day finally ends.

37
00:01:22,950 --> 00:01:23,991
Then you let go.

38
00:01:24,031 --> 00:01:26,761
Time moves forward, soft and unstoppable.

39
00:01:26,801 --> 00:01:29,532
The button sits quietly on the lamp post,

40
00:01:29,572 --> 00:01:32,910
waiting for a moment you would never want to lose.
